WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.912 --> 00:00:17.096
Kopp and weren't the only ones looking for a cure.

2
00:00:18.196 --> 00:00:21.397
The palace servants loved the lighthearted princess.

3
00:00:21.917 --> 00:00:23.878
She made them laugh and feel happy.

4
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.713
know what will help her," a servant told Nanny.

5
00:00:32.733 --> 00:00:36.415
"Falling in love with a handsome prince."

6
00:00:37.836 --> 00:00:38.856
Nanny shook her head.

7
00:00:38.876 --> 00:00:41.338
"Don't you remember?

8
00:00:41.678 --> 00:00:44.279
The princess has no gravity.

9
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.742
She can't fall into anything!"

10
00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:53.324
Actually, reader, the princess was already in love.

11
00:00:55.145 --> 00:00:56.546
But it wasn't with a prince.

12
00:00:57.687 --> 00:00:59.428
It was with the palace's lake.

13
00:01:02.364 --> 00:01:05.406
It started when Ellen accidentally fell in the water.

14
00:01:07.247 --> 00:01:09.309
The family was boating on the lake.

15
00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:13.692
Ellen suddenly spotted a friend's boat across the lake.

16
00:01:18.075 --> 00:01:20.516
I want to go on Mary's boat.

17
00:01:21.577 --> 00:01:22.678
Can you help me?"

18
00:01:22.698 --> 00:01:24.799
"Of course."

19
00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:26.680
The king picked her up.

20
00:01:27.301 --> 00:01:31.243
He carried her to the side of the boat when—boompf!

21
00:01:31.323 --> 00:01:34.301
He tripped, and Ellen splashed into the water.

22
00:01:34.321 --> 00:01:36.302
"She'll drown!"

23
00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:37.423
the king cried.

24
00:01:37.443 --> 00:01:39.244
"She can't swim!"

25
00:01:39.264 --> 00:01:41.145
"I'll save her, Your Majesty!"

26
00:01:41.845 --> 00:01:43.726
A servant dived into the water.

27
00:01:46.748 --> 00:01:50.270
But when the servant came back up, his arms were empty.

28
00:01:52.911 --> 00:01:56.913
A second later the princess popped up—on the other side of the lake.

29
00:01:56.933 --> 00:01:58.975
"Here I am!"

30
00:02:03.989 --> 00:02:05.270
she yelled, laughing.

31
00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:08.891
The servant tried to get her, but she swam away.

32
00:02:10.472 --> 00:02:14.414
For hours, she swam around the lake like a swan.

33
00:02:23.539 --> 00:02:26.000
In the water gravity didn't matter.

34
00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:32.511
For the first time, Ellen felt truly free to move on her own.

35
00:02:34.092 --> 00:02:37.454
After this event all Ellen wanted to do was swim.

36
00:02:39.776 --> 00:02:42.077
In the summer she swam all day long.

37
00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:48.842
In the winter servants broke the ice for her.

38
00:02:53.485 --> 00:02:58.008
At night she stared out her bedroom window, missing the lake.

39
00:03:03.456 --> 00:03:06.138
The philosophers watched Ellen closely.

40
00:03:12.343 --> 00:03:14.705
Soon they both had the same thought.

41
00:03:14.725 --> 00:03:16.106
"That's it!"

42
00:03:16.506 --> 00:03:17.227
Kopp shouted.

43
00:03:17.247 --> 00:03:19.809
"Yes!" Humm cried.

44
00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:23.511
They rushed to tell the king and queen.

45
00:03:23.532 --> 00:03:25.353
"Your Majesties!

46
00:03:26.093 --> 00:03:28.175
We have found a cure for the princess!"

47
00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:29.116
Kopp said.

48
00:03:31.052 --> 00:03:32.193
"A wonderful cure!

49
00:03:32.513 --> 00:03:33.394
It's water!"

50
00:03:33.414 --> 00:03:36.536
"Water?" The king frowned.

51
00:03:36.556 --> 00:03:38.677
"She swims all the time.

52
00:03:38.797 --> 00:03:40.258
Water hasn't cured her yet."

53
00:03:41.199 --> 00:03:43.100
"No," Kopp said impatiently.

54
00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:46.102
"She needs water from inside herself.

55
00:03:46.543 --> 00:03:49.825
The water must come from—" "Tears!"

56
00:03:50.365 --> 00:03:51.006
Humm said.

57
00:03:51.026 --> 00:03:53.828
"We must make Ellen cry!"
